# IP + Billing + Ward + Cross-Module SoT

Canonical doc: `apps/hospital-portal-web/docs/ip-billing-ward-cross-module-sot.md`

This is a production Eye Hospital Management System. Inspect and extend existing architecture. Do not duplicate services, introduce a second framework, or remove functionality unless this prompt requires it or the current implementation is demonstrably wrong.

## Ownership (do not invert)

| Domain | Source of truth | Existing home |
|---|---|---|
| Clinical / operational / admission lifecycle | IP Management `PatientJourney` | `microservices/ip-management-service` |
| Charges, advances, payments, refunds, receipts, settlement | Billing `OpdBill` | Auth `OpdBillService` |
| Coverage, claims, payer responsibility | CCMS | `microservices/ccms-service` |
| Bed occupancy | Auth bed inventory | `InternalIpBedController` / `BedLifecyclePolicy` |
| Realtime | Existing `NotificationHub` | Auth SignalR |
| Cross-module events | Existing integration outbox | `IntegrationOutboxService` |

IP journey financial fields (`FinancialState`, `TotalPaid`, `IpBillingTransaction`, …) are **projections / clinical workflow**, not accounting records. Classify via `IpFinancialFieldClassification`. Do not silently overwrite financial totals. Do not use frontend state as clinical or financial truth.

## Required process

- Trace every change FE → API → BE → DB → integrations.
- Validate every business-critical state transition server-side.
- Make every financial operation auditable.
- Preserve backward compatibility where practical.
- Complete required work across frontend, backend, database, APIs, integrations, and tests — not UI-only.
- After each phase: build, lint, type-check, migration validation, unit/integration/existing tests. Fix issues you introduce before completing the phase.

## Phase close-out (required)

files changed · database changes · APIs changed/added · integrations changed · tests added/updated · remaining risks · exact validation commands
